Z||000000||Banzai||12-26-2001||10:53 AM||||The tranny in my resto. 84 is leaking. Even  Before I filled  it I was getting  a small amount of oil seeping on the bottom of the  tranny. Now, after a couple hundred miles of shakedown, there is oil all over. I replaced the output seals before I put it back together. Some oil is coming from the shift shaft area, where can I get a new  seal? This doesn't explain the seeping before I filled the tranny. Is there an area I should look for cracks?? I didn't see any when I was prepping and painting the tranny. PLEASE HELP!!<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||12-26-2001||11:02 AM||||<BR>A while back I replaced the output shaft seals on my 4-speed and... it leaked.  WHAT?!!!<P>Found out when I pulled it apart... again, that the dumb schmuck of a mechanic before me scored the inner lip of the shaft opening while using his "seal removal tool."<P>I did this to stop the leak:<BR>1) I cleaned up the shaft area<BR>2) I ran a very small bead of rtv along the inside edge (so when you tap in the seal in fills in the scores)<BR>3) tapped in a new seal<BR>4) have not had problems since<P>Note<BR>Be careful with the quantity of rtv used, you really don't want rtv in the gears of the tranny.<P>BTW, you can purchase output shaft seals at just about any local auto parts place (i.e. auto zone).<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 12-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Banzai||12-27-2001||12:16 AM||||Thanks Gold, I'll check it out.<P>Banzai!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
